response:
 First, notice $5^{a_{n + 1} - a_n} = 1 + \frac {1}{n + \frac {2}{3}}  = \frac {n + \frac{5}{3}}{n + \frac{2}{3}}$. Second, notice 
\begin{align*}
\sum_{n=1}^{k} (n + \frac{5}{3}) - \sum_{n=1}^{k} (n + \frac{2}{3}) = k(k + \frac{5}{3}) - k(k + \frac{2}{3}).  
\end{align*}
Third, notice 
\begin{align*}
a_{k+1} - a_1 & =  \sum_{x = 1}^k (x + \frac{5}{3}) - \sum_{x=1}^{k} (x + \frac{2}{3} ) \\
& = \sum_{n = 2}^{k+1} n \\
& = \frac{k(k +3)}{2} - 1.
\end{align*}
Fourth, $2(a_{k+1} - a_1) + 2 = k(k + 3)$ always includes 2 as factor. Thus $k = 3$.\ </think> <answer>$3$</answer>

